CloudBurrow patch 5 of 6 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061).

The bug: googlesqlite v0.3.1 registers no googlesqlite_unary_minus, the
function the - operator on one operand formats to, so `SELECT -a FROM ...`,
and any negation the analyzer does not fold into a literal, failed "no such
function: googlesqlite_unary_minus". The patch registers it: an INT64 stays
an INT64 (the negation of its minimum overflows, as in GoogleSQL), a FLOAT64
a FLOAT64, and a NUMERIC or BIGNUMERIC keeps its type; NULL is NULL.
unary_minus_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

